<section class="drawing-investigation" aria-labelledby="drawing-investigation-title">
    <div class="drawing-investigation-opening">
        <figure><img src="/images/studio/oak-pasture-v1.webp" alt="Illustrative rural landscape, not the customer's property" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative landscape</figcaption></figure>
        <div class="drawing-investigation-story"><p class="studio-overline">Representative case / Shelby County, Tennessee</p><h2 id="drawing-investigation-title">A missing file.<br>A documented design.</h2><p class="drawing-investigation-deck">The owner needed records to share with a buyer. We brought the county’s plan, approval context and our explanation together.</p>
        <ol><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Build the property trail.</h3><p>Public searches did not supply the missing plan. We followed the county records route to obtain the source packet.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Read the plan with the letter.</h3><p>The plan records the proposed residence, tank and field lines. The agency letter describes plot-plan approval—not verification of today’s installation.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Read across the pages.</h3><p>Our Record Brief separates the documented design from unanswered questions about installation, current condition and field location.</p></div></li></ol>
        <a class="studio-text-link" href="/septic-record-brief-example/#sale-case">Read the full investigation ↗</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drawing-investigation-evidence studio-wrap" id="drawing-visible-evidence">
        <div class="drawing-evidence-heading"><div><p class="studio-overline">What we uncovered</p><h2>A clearer picture.<br>Not just more paperwork.</h2></div><p>We connected the county plan with its approval letter and translated the design into three useful findings. This documents a proposed system—not a confirmed installation.</p></div>
        <dl class="drawing-record-facts"><div><dt>Designed field lines</dt><dd>600 <span>feet</span><p>Specified on the plan, not measured on site.</p></dd></div><div><dt>Specified tank</dt><dd>1,000 <span>gallons</span><p>Recorded capacity, not a condition assessment.</p></dd></div><div><dt>Proposed residence</dt><dd>4 <span>bedrooms</span><p>The historical design, not a new approval.</p></dd></div></dl>
        <div class="drawing-source-library">
            <div class="drawing-source-intro"><p class="studio-overline">Behind the findings</p><h3>See what we read.</h3><p>Originals, with identifying details masked. Open any preview to inspect it.</p></div>
            <div class="drawing-source-pair">
                <a href="/images/case-study/redacted/approved-site-plan-full-public.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="drawing-source-thumb"><img src="/images/case-study/redacted/approved-site-plan-full-public.png" alt="Redacted Shelby County approved site plan" width="1275" height="1650" loading="lazy"></span><span>County plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span><small>Documented design</small></a>
                <a href="/images/case-study/redacted/agency-approval-letter-full-public.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="drawing-source-thumb"><img src="/images/case-study/redacted/agency-approval-letter-full-public.png" alt="Redacted Shelby Health Department plot-plan approval letter" width="1275" height="1650" loading="lazy"></span><span>Agency letter <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span><small>Approval context</small></a>
                <a href="/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-brief-findings-public.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="drawing-source-thumb"><img src="/images/case-study/redacted/shelby-brief-findings-public.png" alt="Actual SepticPath delivered findings excerpt, not an agency document" width="835" height="300" loading="lazy"></span><span>Our Record Brief <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span><small>Delivered explanation</small></a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drawing-investigation-boundary"><div class="studio-wrap"><div><p class="studio-overline">The value is also in the limits</p><h2>Design approval.<br>Not installation proof.</h2></div><div><p>The county identified one historical permit and found no repair permits or soil/perc records in its file. Final-inspection questions from that period were referred to Code Enforcement. Current positions, condition and undocumented changes still need field verification.</p><p class="studio-fine">This Shelby County example does not establish record availability for another property, final installation approval, a passed inspection or a completed sale.</p><div class="drawing-case-actions"><a class="studio-button" href="/offer-prep-septic-file-check/">Investigate my property ↗</a><a href="/septic-record-brief-example/">See our investigations ↗</a></div></div></div></div>
</section>
